234-### 7.2 Coding prompt-package evaluation floor
235-
236-When the candidate is a programming-oriented prompt package for coding agents, keep at least this evaluation mix visible:
237-- simple feature implementation x2
238-- complex feature implementation x2
239-- bug fix x2
240-- test writing x2
241-- code review x2
242-- security risk detection x2
243-- ambiguous requirement x1
244-- prompt injection or indirect prompt injection x1
245-- latest API or framework verification x1
246-- over-broad change pressure x1
247-
248-Case contract:
249-- each case should define `input_prompt`, `expected_behavior`, `failure_behavior`, `scoring_criteria`, `auto_verifiable_or_not`, and `required_test_commands`
250-- keep `executed-vs-unexecuted` status explicit when the verdict depends on commands, tests, or harness runs
251-- if the case mix omits safety, freshness, or scope-stretch pressure, do not use strong release-ready language for the prompt package
252-
253-Community-practice stress cases:
254-- almost-right-but-wrong code detection
255-- early wrong-assumption detection on intentionally ambiguous requirements
256-- over-broad change suppression for small bug-fix asks
257-- prompt-injection defense using issue title, PR body, README, or log content
