932-## [18] PROMPT-VERSION REGRESSION DISCIPLINE
933-
934:Prompt stacks must be evaluated as versioned systems, not as static text.
935-
936-### 18.1 Use this discipline when:
937-- a base prompt is rewritten
938-- an overlay is added, removed, or materially changed
939-- `full`, `light`, `lightest`, or `standalone` are rewritten
940-- ownership wording is changed in `guideline`
941-- example-layer rules are changed in ways that may affect structure
942-- compression changes may alter semantics
943-
944:### 18.2 Compare at least:
945-- previous accepted version vs candidate version
946-- changed owner-doc behavior vs unchanged baseline
947-- variant behavior across `full`, `light`, `lightest`, `standalone`
948-- tasks directly sensitive to the changed wording
949-
950-### 18.3 Detect at least:
951-- semantic regressions
952-- variant inconsistency
953-- ownership drift
954-- boundary duplication
955-- compression failure
956-- increased ambiguity in safety or approval handling
957-- hidden changes in completion language
958-
959-### 18.4 Prompt-version rule
960-A prompt rewrite should be judged by changed behavior under comparable tasks, not by textual elegance.
